# Counter-example: a lang:Grapheme admitted to the GMN script (lang:inScript gmeow:gmnScript)
# with a canonical codepoint-explicit spelling but NO gmeow:gmnGlyphTokenCost — no measured
# per-glyph token-cost feed dispositioning it in the glyph plane. GMN glyph-cost coverage is
# total, so a script glyph missing its cost feed is a silent gap (fires
# lang:GmnUncostedScriptGlyph via the sh:sparql of lang:GmnScriptGlyphCoverageShape). It is
# otherwise well-formed — grounded in the script's repertoire and canonically spelled — so no
# other shape fires.

@prefix lang:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/lang/> .

gmeow:gmnScript lang:hasGrapheme ex:gUncosted .

ex:gUncosted a lang:Grapheme ;
    lang:inScript gmeow:gmnScript ;
    gmeow:gmnCodepoints "U+0294" .
